From: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] net: core: optimize NAPI budget and backlog queue bounds for multi-gigabit routing

================================================================================
MAXNET High-Performance Kernel Engine & Hardware Architecture Optimization
Engineered & Developed by Mahendra Mali (Max) for MAXNET Router OS
Copyright (c) 2026 Mahendra Mali - Max. All Rights Reserved.
================================================================================

On Qualcomm IPQ9574 / IPQ9554 enterprise quad-core networking gateways, the
platform processes multi-gigabit line-rate traffic across 2.5G SGMII/PSGMII ports,
Wi-Fi 6 160MHz channels, and 5Gbps SuperSpeed USB 3.0 mobile interfaces.

Under default Linux kernel networking thresholds:
- netdev_budget (300 packets) forces premature NAPI polling termination during
  heavy ingress packet bursts, triggering repeated softirq wakeups and context switches.
- netdev_max_backlog (1000 packets) drops frames under concurrent multi-client
  RPS (Receive Packet Steering) hashing.

This MAXNET acceleration patch:
1. Scales initial netdev_budget from 300 to 600 packets and netdev_budget_usecs
   to 4000us, maximizing ingress ring processing efficiency on A73 cores.
2. Increases default netdev_max_backlog from 1000 to 4096 packets, eliminating
   backlog ring drops during gigabit burst forwarding.

Signed-off-by: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
---
 net/core/dev.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/net/core/dev.c
+++ b/net/core/dev.c
@@ -4329,9 +4329,15 @@
 /* The NAPI poll-list has an entry for each device which needs to be
  * processed.
  */
-int netdev_budget __read_mostly = 300;
+/* MAXNET Network Acceleration Engine by Mahendra Mali (Max):
+ * High-throughput NAPI and backlog defaults for multi-gigabit routing
+ */
+int netdev_budget __read_mostly = 600;
+unsigned int __read_mostly netdev_budget_usecs = 4000;
+int netdev_max_backlog __read_mostly = 4096;
+
 /* Must be at least 2 jiffies to guarantee we observe a tick boundary */
-unsigned int __read_mostly netdev_budget_usecs = 2000;
-int netdev_max_backlog __read_mostly = 1000;
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(netdev_max_backlog);
 
 /* Device queue lock class */
